{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778522406,"nonce":"Am5SZjbK+LtbOidQbz7LkZbLwBA=","title":"Auto-rebuild Mandible on post-merge / post-pull (eliminate manual build step)","message":"After every `git pull` or merge that touches TypeScript source, Mandible's daemon + channel-server need to be rebuilt before they reflect the new code. This is currently manual (`npm run build` / `npm run build:channel-server`), and easy to forget — leading to stale built JS running silently against fresh sources.\n\nSurfaced from `497fafa` discussion: the channel-server in particular is registered as a Claude Code MCP server via a path to `dist/channel-server/index.js`. If the source is updated but not rebuilt, every new Claude Code session runs stale code with no warning.\n\n## Options\n\n1. **Git post-merge / post-rewrite hook** installed via Mandible's setup script (or a bootstrap step). Auto-runs `npm run build` (or a smart subset) when any tracked TypeScript file changed in the diff.\n2. **`prestart` npm script** that compares dist freshness vs source mtimes and rebuilds if stale. Adds a small startup check but no separate hook to install.\n3. **Watcher process** during `npm run dev` (already exists) — only solves the dev case, not the post-pull case.\n\nOption 1 is most reliable for the merge-then-forget case. Option 2 covers more entry points (any `npm start`, including channel-server spawn) but adds latency to every spawn. They could combine.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Tauri sidecar bundling: that path ships prebuilt JS, independent of this.\n- Worktree-specific TS errors (issue `61778cb`).\n\n## Cross-refs\n\n- Surfaced from `497fafa` (dotfiles → Mandible script migration), specifically the rebuild-footgun discussion.\n- Tangentially relates to `61778cb` (worktree TS baseline).\n- rlrmp meta coord: `1d9ae6f`.","files":null}]}